cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ΔM-Antigravity: A Numerical Model of Repulsive Force Between Nested Mass Layers"
abstract: >
  A numerical model in which the force between two nested mass layers
  contains a repulsive term proportional to the mass difference ΔM.
  The model is regularized by a tanh function and yields a stable
  equilibrium at radius r_eq, which scales as r_eq ∝ (M/ΔM)^(1/3).
  Unlike the cosmological constant Λ, the effect is local and depends
  only on local masses. The reference implementation is written in
  Python (NumPy only) and includes numerical verification of the
  equilibrium radius scaling. Research prototype (TRL 3). Not a
  physical theory, not experimentally validated.
